  <h1 class="wmd-h1">Wireframe: Location Switcher &amp; Saved Locations</h1>
<blockquote class="wmd-blockquote">
  <p class="wmd-paragraph"><strong>Screen:</strong> 13 | <strong>Status:</strong> Draft | <strong>Updated:</strong> 2026-02-19
<strong>Journey:</strong> <a href="../user-journeys/location/01-location-permission-and-detection.md">01-location-permission-and-detection</a> - Scenario D
<strong>Feature:</strong> <a href="../features/dynamic-location-management.md">dynamic-location-management</a> - Features L.5, L.6
<strong>Story:</strong> As a commuter with multiple locations, I want to quickly switch between my saved locations to view feeds from different metro areas.
<strong>Platforms:</strong> Mobile + Web</p>
</blockquote>
<hr class="wmd-separator" />
<h2 class="wmd-h2">Screen Purpose + Key Goals</h2>
<p class="wmd-paragraph">The location switcher is triggered by tapping the metro name in the home screen header. It provides quick access to saved locations, current GPS-detected location, and the ability to add/manage locations.</p>
<p class="wmd-paragraph"><strong>Key Goals:</strong></p>
<ul class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Enable fast switching between saved locations (1 tap)</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Show current GPS-detected location when it differs from active location</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Provide entry points to add new locations and manage existing ones</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Keep it lightweight — this is a quick-access panel, not a full screen</li>
</ul>
<hr class="wmd-separator" />
<h2 class="wmd-h2">Visual Wireframe</h2>
