<h2 class="wmd-h2">User Interactions</h2>
<h3 class="wmd-h3">Primary Flow — Receiving a Chat Notification (Mobile Push)</h3>
<ol class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User is in background or device locked</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Expo Push sends notification via APNs/FCM</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">System shows banner: &quot;Rajan Thapa: Hey, is the room still availab...&quot;</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User taps → app opens → navigates directly to MessageThreadScreen with Rajan</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Notification marked as read automatically</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="wmd-h3">Primary Flow — Receiving a Chat Notification (Web Push)</h3>
<ol class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User has browser open (different tab or minimized)</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Service worker receives push event via Web Push API</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Browser shows OS notification: &quot;Nepally — Rajan Thapa: Hey, is the room...&quot;</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User clicks → browser focuses Nepally tab → navigates to /messages/:conversationId</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Notification marked as read</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="wmd-h3">Primary Flow — In-App Bell Dropdown (Web)</h3>
<ol class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User clicks bell icon in nav</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Dropdown opens with last 8 notifications, sorted newest first</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Unread items shown with blue left border + unread background</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User clicks a notification → navigates to source content → dropdown closes</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Notification marked as read</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">&quot;Mark all as read&quot; → all items turn read state</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">&quot;See all notifications →&quot; → navigates to /notifications full page</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="wmd-h3">Primary Flow — Viewing Notifications List (Mobile)</h3>
<ol class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User taps &quot;Alerts&quot; tab in bottom tab bar</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Notifications list loads, grouped by day</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Emergency alerts pinned at top</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Unread items shown with blue dot + tinted background</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User taps item → navigates to source (chat, post, etc.)</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Notification auto-marked as read on tap</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Swipe left on item → &quot;Dismiss&quot; red button → removes from list</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="wmd-h3">Primary Flow — Enabling Push (Mobile First Launch)</h3>
<ol class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User opens app for first time (or after sign-in)</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">System modal shown: &quot;Stay in the Loop&quot;</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User taps &quot;Allow Notifications&quot; → OS permission dialog (iOS/Android) shown</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">On allow: device token registered in device_tokens table, linked to user</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">On deny: banner shown in-app for next 3 sessions offering to re-enable</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="wmd-h3">Primary Flow — Enabling Browser Push (Web)</h3>
<ol class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User signs in to web app</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">After 30s delay, soft prompt shown: &quot;Enable Push Notifications&quot;</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">User clicks &quot;Enable Push&quot; → browser permission dialog</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">On allow: service worker subscribes, push subscription stored server-side</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">On deny: no repeat prompt for 7 days</li>
</ol>
<h3 class="wmd-h3">Alternative Flows</h3>
<ul class="wmd-list">
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Chat active (mobile): Supabase Realtime delivers message in-app; push NOT sent if user is currently viewing that conversation (suppress logic)</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Emergency alert: Always delivered via push regardless of preferences, shown first in list with red styling</li>
  <li class="wmd-list-item">Preferences change: User disables &quot;Likes&quot; → no new like notifications from that point, existing ones remain in list</li>
</ul>
